SE: The 'username' input value is directly concatenated into the 'register' object without proper sanitization.
BL: var register = {
			textroom: "join",
			transaction: transaction,
			room: myroom,
			username: myid,
			display: username
		};

SE: The 'fields[title]' and 'fields[handle]' values are directly concatenated into error messages without proper sanitation, which may lead to a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.
BL: $this->_errors['title'] = __('This is a required field');
BL: $this->_errors['handle'] = __('A page with that handle already exists');

SE: The 'label' and 'bank' fields are directly concatenated into the HTML content without sanitation, which may lead to a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.

BL: `print '<tr><td class="titlefield fieldrequired">'.$langs->trans("LabelRIB").'</td>';
print '<td colspan="4"><input size="30" type="text" name="label" value="'.$account->label.'"></td></tr>';

print '<tr><td class="fieldrequired">'.$langs->trans("BankName").'</td>';
print '<td><input size="30" type="text" name="bank" value="'.$account->bank.'"></td></tr>';`

SE: The user input from $_REQUEST['QSType'] and $_REQUEST['QuickSearch'] is not properly sanitized before being used in the code, which may lead to a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.

BL: $qs_type = strip_tags($_REQUEST['QSType']);
$qs_text = strip_tags($_REQUEST['QuickSearch']);

SE: The 'message' variable is passed to the 'dangerouslySetInnerHTML' prop without proper sanitization, which may lead to a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.

BL: 
```jsx
dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
  __html: DOMPurify.sanitize(renderMarkdown(message)),
}}
```

SE: The 'node_type', 'node_cidr', 'node_domain', and 'node_description' variables are directly concatenated into the HTML content without sanitation, which may lead to a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.
BL: 
```php
echo "	<td valign='top' class='".$row_style[$c]."'>".escape($row['node_type'])."&nbsp;</td>\n";
echo "	<td valign='top' class='".$row_style[$c]."'><a ".$tr_link.">".escape($row['node_cidr'])."</a></td>\n";
echo "	<td valign='top' class='".$row_style[$c]."'>".escape($row['node_domain'])."&nbsp;</td>\n";
echo "	<td valign='top' class='".$row_style[$c]."'>".escape($row['node_description'])."&nbsp;</td>\n";
```

SE: The 'action' field in the propertiesColumns array is directly concatenated into the HTML content without sanitation.
BL: {text: t("action"), width: 100, sortable: false, dataIndex: 'action', editor: new Ext.form.ComboBox({
                    triggerAction: 'all',
                    editable: false,
                    store: actionTypes,
                    displayField:'name',
                    valueField: "key",
                    mode: 'local'
                }),renderer: function(value, metaData, record, rowIndex, colIndex, store, view) {
                    try {
                        var rec = actionTypes.findRecord("key", value);
                        if (rec) {
                            return rec.get("name");
                        }
                    }
                    catch (e) {
                        console.log(e);

                    }

                    return "";
                }}

